  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Elephant conservation and education campaigns and capacity strengthening of future protected area managers in the Western Forest Complex, Thailand - Year 7</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to maintain the SMART patrol system in Thung Yai West Wildlife Sanctuary (TYW) at its current intensity and coverage and to build a volunteer network in Huai Kha Khaeng (HKK) from existing volunteer groups and university conservation clubs. Project activities will include: 1) conduct follow-up monitoring with 17 patrol teams in TYW by providing technical support, refresher training, equipment, and patrol rations; 2) entry, review, and analysis of patrol data into the SMART database; 3) prepare and distribute monthly SMART reports; and 4) build a volunteer network by selecting a group of 40 volunteers, including local school teachers, NGOs, and Thai university students to participate in a 5-day wildlife conservation workshop at HKK. This project will contribute to the protection and increase of the wild population of Asian elephants in Thailands Western Forest Complex, a UNESCO Natural World Heritage Site.</narrative>
  </description>
